भ॑ग m. distributer, dispenser, gracious lord, protector,
N. of an Āditya & E. of sev. gods;
 portion, lot, fortune;
 abundance.
happiness;
 dignity, majesty;
 loveliness, beauty;
 affection, love;
 the
vulva.

1 भाग॑ m. part, portion, share, property;
 lot, esp. happy
lot, good fortune;
 place, spot, region, side.

भगवद्गीत a. sung or declared by Bhagavant i.e.
Kṛṣṇa;
 f. आ pl. (±उपनिषद्) T. of a philosophical poem.

भागि॑न् a. sharing in, partaking of, responsible for,
entitled to (loc., gen., or —˚);
 m. partaker, owner.

भागीरथ f. ई relating to Bhagīratha;
 f. ई E. of
Gaṅgā.

भग्न a. broken, bent, curved;
 scattered, defeated,
disappointed, marred, destroyed, annihilated, lost;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

भागधे॑य n. portion, share, property;
 lot, esp.
happy lot, luck, fortune;
 a. (f. ई) due as a share.

भागवत f. ई relating to Bhagavant (Viṣṇu), m. a
follower of Bh.;
 n. = seq.

भागशस् adv. in parts, part by part;
 in turns, by and
by.

2 भाग्य a. lucky, fortunate;
 n. lot, fortune, welfare,
reward, fate, destiny.
